 compatible source commit for repeatable tests; the development branch and web renderer can differ from stable desktop behavior.","limitations","guidance","list","Setup","ordered",true,"items",[73,74,75],"setup","Choose a stable demo branch or release compatible with the installed Godot version; pin its commit.","Download one demo directory, import its project.godot and run its main scene.","Save the engine version, scene, input sequence and expected result alongside the baseline.","Try these tasks",false,[80,81,82],"testTasks","Change one movement or collision rule and verify the original scene still starts and completes its objective.","Import a known model or animation, then compare material loading, scale, skeleton mapping and exported behavior.","Replay the same input sequence and record screenshots, errors and task completion.","AI use and evaluation boundary","A useful open-license baseline for code editing and automated playtests. Record licenses of any additional assets or plugins rather than treating the demo license as a grant for unrelated data.","aiUseNote","links","Supporting evidence",[90,91,92],"evidence",{"_54":97,"_25":98},{"_54":95,"_25":96},{"_54":93,"_25":94},"Repository license","https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/blob/master/LICENSE.md","Official browser builds","https://godotengine.github.io/godot-demo-projects/","Official source and branch guidance","https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects","Read the terms",[102],"licenseUrl",{"_54":99,"_25":94},"Terms category","Open-license sources","terms","provenance","Asset license","Repository MIT license applies unless an individual demo or bundled resource states otherwise; keep local attribution notices.","assetLicense","Code license","MIT; retain the repository license and notices.","codeLicense","Get started",[116],"access",{"_54":117,"_25":96,"_118":119},"Play browser demos","note","Free browser builds and downloadable source projects. Browser exports cover a subset of 